  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1227 PM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nWe continue our quiet weather pattern with a continued warmup into \nthe low to mid 70s expected through Saturday before a surface low \ndeepens as its moves eastward across northwest TX. A frontal \nboundary attached to this low is expected to make its way over our \narea late Saturday night into early Sunday morning. Most model \nguidance has this front coming through dry with most moisture \nremaining trapped across South Texas instead. Regardless we still do \nhave some low end pops (20-30%) across our far southern areas that \ncould see some of this moisture result in a few showers out ahead of \nthis frontal boundary. However widespread rain like we saw this past \nweekend is not expected. \n\nAnother cold front possibly stronger will send another reinforcing\nshot of colder air across our area Monday into Tuesday. Highs \nbehind this front look to struggle to even make it out of the 60s \nwith only upper 50s possible for highs as we get to the middle of \nnext week. For Thanksgiving Day it may be quite a cool one with \nhighs really struggling to get out of the low 50s. Lows during \nthis timeframe will be in the upper 30s but if trends continue we \ncould see our first freeze of the season. For those that have \ntravel plans be sure to keep an eye on the forecast as we continue\nto get closer to next week.",
